Date: Fri, 22 Jan 93 10:06:32 PST
From: Robin Hanson <hanson@ptolemy.arc.nasa.gov>
Subject: Monopolies 

Natural monopolies, or even state-created monopolies, should *not*
result in lazziness or sloppy inattention to the customer *if* the
managers of the monopoly are sufficiently accountable to their owners.
Someone who thinks they should be able to run the monopoly better
should be able to replace the management, by buying out the previous
owners if needed, and this sort of competition can keep monopolies on
their toes.  The real problem is when states limit management
accountability mechanisms, preventing hostile takeovers, and
forbidding someone else to buy a utility and run it however they like.

Robin Hanson

